>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `remove_iff`

``` hol4
clasimpLib.remove_iff : string -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes a persistent `[iff]` declaration by theorem name.

`remove_iff name` records a removal in the current theory and retracts both
the derived classical rules and the `srw_ss()` rewrite. The name is resolved
against the `[iff]` declarations currently installed, whichever theory made
them, so an unqualified name reaches an ancestor's declaration; the
qualified forms `"myTheory.my_iff"` and `"myTheory$my_iff"` name one
declaration outright.

Removal is part of the theory's persistent iff declaration stream and is
therefore replayed and inherited through theory ancestry. It does not
delete the theorem from the theorem database.

Use `BasicProvers.delsimps ["Thy.name.__clasimp_iff"]` instead when only the
simpset view should be removed and the derived classical rules should remain
available.

### Failure

Fails if the name matches no installed `[iff]` declaration, or matches more
than one; nothing is recorded in either case, since the recorded name is
what every descendant theory replays.

### Example

``` hol4
clasimpLib.remove_iff "my_iff";
```

